.TITLE "del"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Deletes one or more files. It permanently removes specified files from the disk and is a standard tool for __cleanup__ and __file management__.

.DIV "ALIAS"
**erase**

.DIV "TLDR"
**del file**
Deletes the specified file from the current directory.
> __file__ the target file name

**del *.txt**
Deletes all files with the .txt extension in the current directory.
> __*.txt__ wildcard for text files

**del /p file**
Prompts for confirmation before deleting each file.
> __/p__ prompt flag

**del /f file**
Forces the deletion of read-only files.
> __/f__ force flag

**del /s *.log**
Deletes specified files from all subdirectories.
> __/s__ subdirectory flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Use the __/p__ flag when using wildcards to avoid accidental deletion of important data. Files deleted with __del__ are not sent to the Recycle Bin and cannot be easily recovered.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**windows:rmdir** **windows:copy**

documentation: __https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/del__
